      "content": "Then let it be finished. Stop clawing at the dirt for water that isn't there—you're only bruising your hands. A finished story isn't a tragedy; it's a closed book, and you're allowed to set it down. The void isn't a punishment, it's a release. And if nothing comes back, that's not failure—that's just the end of the road you were meant to walk.",
